---
// Landing page (/). The value narrative moves from the problem (agent behaviour can't be compared or
// trusted across vendors) to the consequence (unverifiable claims, risk carried into production) to the
// resolution (a shared, executable conformance standard that produces reproducible evidence). Copy is
// grounded in what the engine actually does; the terminal is generated from a real quickstart run (scripts/quickstart-hero.mjs).
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const features = [
  {
    title: 'Deterministic',
    body: 'No learned component decides an outcome. The same evidence and rules produce the same verdict on every run, on every machine.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Model-free evidence',
    body: 'The engine reads structured evidence and evaluates it against explicit rules. What it cannot verify, it reports as insufficient — it never guesses.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Vendor-neutral',
    body: 'One specification and one control catalog. Agents and frameworks are assessed on the same terms, so a result means the same thing everywhere.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Reproducible',
    body: 'Reports have a canonical byte form. Independent engines in Python, TypeScript, and Java produce identical output over the same inputs.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Verifiable',
    body: 'Implementation reports and catalogs are signed and content-addressed. Evidence checks out against its source — claims you can confirm, not take on faith.',
  },
  {
    title: 'CI-ready',
    body: 'Scriptable, exit-code driven, and runnable with networking disabled. Assess an agent on every change before it reaches production.',
  },
];

const artifacts = [
  { name: 'assertions.json', note: 'one machine-readable verdict per control and subject — the source of truth' },
  { name: 'report.md · report.html', note: 'the human-readable report, each finding citing its evidence' },
  { name: 'results.sarif', note: 'findings in SARIF for code-scanning and CI surfaces' },
  { name: 'oscal-ar.json', note: 'an OSCAL Assessment Results rendering for GRC tooling' },
];
---

<BaseLayout title="Agent Conformance — a standard for how AI agents behave">
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">The open conformance standard for AI agents</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">Prove how your agents behave — the same way, across every vendor.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Agent Conformance is a deterministic, model-free assessment standard: one executable
        specification, conforming engines in several languages, and byte-identical evidence you can
        verify. A claim about an agent means the same thing no matter who makes it.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="/docs/getting-started/">Get started</a>
        <a class="button" href="https://github.com/agent-conformance/agentce">View on GitHub</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <figure class="terminal" aria-label="Running an assessment with the command-line engine">
      <div class="terminal-bar" aria-hidden="true">
        <span></span><span></span><span></span>
      </div>
      {/* quickstart-run:begin — generated by scripts/quickstart-hero.mjs, do not edit by hand */}
      <pre><code><span class="c-prompt">$</span> <span class="c-cmd">agentce quickstart --out ./out</span>
quickstart complete: 49 assertions; report in ./out

<span class="c-prompt">$</span> <span class="c-cmd">head -n 10 out/report.md</span>
# AgentCE conformance report

## Outcome summary

- conformant: 25
- non-conformant: 0
- partial: 0
- not applicable: 0
- not assessed: 5
- insufficient evidence: 19</code></pre>
      <figcaption>
        The real output of that command over the bundled <code>corpus/quickstart</code> project: 25 conformant, 19 insufficient evidence, 5 not assessed, of 49 controls.
        Insufficient evidence means a control applies and was evaluated, but the evidence collected did not meet its minimum;
        it is a gap in what was collected, not a failure and not a guess.
      </figcaption>
      {/* quickstart-run:end */}
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="band narrative" aria-labelledby="why-title">
    <div class="inner">
      <h2 id="why-title">Agent behaviour is hard to compare, and harder to trust.</h2>
      <div class="narrative-grid">
        <div>
          <h3>The problem</h3>
          <p>
            Every framework describes its agent differently, and most evidence about how an agent
            actually behaved never leaves the vendor. There is no common way to ask whether two agents
            meet the same bar.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>The consequence</h3>
          <p>
            Assurances become claims you cannot check. Risk that should be caught before release is
            carried into production, and obligations under frameworks like the EU AI Act are met on
            paper rather than in evidence.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>The resolution</h3>
          <p>
            A shared, executable standard. The engine collects evidence about an agent, evaluates it
            against a public control catalog, and produces a report anyone can reproduce and verify —
            the same result, independently.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="features-title">
    <div class="inner">
      <h2 id="features-title">Built to be trusted, not just believed.</h2>
      <ul class="feature-grid">
        {
          features.map((f) => (
            <li>
              <h3>{f.title}</h3>
              <p>{f.body}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band artifacts" aria-labelledby="artifacts-title">
    <div class="inner">
      <h2 id="artifacts-title">One run, every rendering an adopter needs.</h2>
      <p class="band-lede">
        A single assessment writes the same evidence in the forms your tools already read — a machine
        verdict, a human report, and standard security and governance renderings.
      </p>
      <ul class="artifact-list">
        {
          artifacts.map((a) => (
            <li>
              <code>{a.name}</code>
              <span>{a.note}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band cta" aria-labelledby="cta-title">
    <div class="inner">
      <h2 id="cta-title">Assess your first agent in a few minutes.</h2>
      <p class="band-lede">
        Run the bundled example end to end, then point the engine at your own agent. Everything is open
        source and Apache-2.0 licensed.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="/docs/getting-started/">Read the docs</a>
        <a class="button" href="https://github.com/agent-conformance/agentce">Browse the source</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .inner {
      max-width: var(--measure);
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 0 1.5rem;
    }
    .band {
      padding: 4rem 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
    .band h2 {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3.5vw, 2.1rem);
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
      margin: 0 0 2rem;
      max-width: 24ch;
    }
    .band-lede {
      color: var(--text-muted);
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      max-width: 60ch;
      margin: -1rem 0 2rem;
    }

    /* Hero */
    .hero {
      max-width: var(--measure);
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 4.5rem 1.5rem 3rem;
      display: grid;
      gap: 3rem;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      align-items: center;
    }
    @media (min-width: 60rem) {
      .hero {
        grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 0.95fr;
      }
    }
    .eyebrow {
      color: var(--accent-strong);
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.02em;
      margin: 0 0 1rem;
    }
    .hero h1 {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.3rem);
      line-height: 1.08;
      letter-spacing: -0.025em;
      margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
      max-width: 18ch;
    }
    .lede {
      font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2vw, 1.2rem);
      color: var(--text-muted);
      max-width: 60ch;
      margin: 0 0 2rem;
    }
    .actions {
      display: flex;
      gap: 0.75rem;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }
    .button {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      padding: 0.7rem 1.3rem;
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
      color: var(--text);
      text-decoration: none;
      font-weight: 500;
      transition: border-color 0.15s ease, background-color 0.15s ease;
    }
    .button.primary {
      background: var(--accent);
      border-color: var(--accent);
      color: var(--accent-contrast);
    }
    .button:hover {
      border-color: var(--accent-strong);
    }
    .button.primary:hover {
      background: var(--accent-strong);
    }

    /* Terminal */
    .terminal {
      margin: 0;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      background: var(--bg-raised);
      box-shadow: 0 20px 45px -30px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.55);
      overflow: hidden;
    }
    .terminal-bar {
      display: flex;
      gap: 0.4rem;
      padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
      background: var(--bg-subtle);
    }
    .terminal-bar span {
      width: 0.7rem;
      height: 0.7rem;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: var(--border-strong);
    }
    .terminal pre {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 1.25rem;
      overflow-x: auto;
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.86rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
      color: var(--text);
    }
    .terminal figcaption {
      padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
      background: var(--bg-subtle);
      font-size: 0.86rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: var(--text-muted);
    }
    .terminal figcaption code {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      color: var(--text);
    }
    .c-prompt { color: var(--text-faint); }
    .c-cmd { color: var(--accent-strong); font-weight: 600; }

    /* Narrative */
    .narrative-grid {
      display: grid;
      gap: 2rem;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr));
    }
    .narrative-grid h3 {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
      color: var(--accent-strong);
    }
    .narrative-grid p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--text-muted);
    }

    /* Features */
    .feature-grid {
      list-style: none;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      display: grid;
      gap: 1.75rem 2.5rem;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr));
    }
    .feature-grid h3 {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: 1.15rem;
      margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    }
    .feature-grid p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--text-muted);
    }

    /* Artifacts */
    .artifacts {
      background: var(--bg-subtle);
    }
    .artifact-list {
      list-style: none;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      display: grid;
      gap: 1rem;
    }
    .artifact-list li {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      align-items: baseline;
      gap: 0.5rem 1rem;
      padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      background: var(--bg-raised);
    }
    .artifact-list code {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      color: var(--accent-strong);
      font-weight: 600;
    }
    .artifact-list span {
      color: var(--text-muted);
    }

    /* CTA */
    .cta .inner {
      text-align: center;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: center;
    }
    .cta .actions {
      justify-content: center;
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
